138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (Under a 2020 congressional appropriations requirement, ICE publishes and periodically updates a detention statistics workbook covering every facility holding at least one detainee: length of stay, inspection status, and the number of beds guaranteed under contract regardless of occupancy. Separately, the agency reports removals, book-ins, and other enforcement metrics on a rolling basis. This report analyzes both the ICE-published workbook and a second, more granular dataset \(individual-level arrest and detention records obtained via FOIA by the Deportation Data Project at UC Berkeley and UCLA\) to build a data-driven picture of enforcement activity under the second Trump administration.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
