1071 0 obj
<<
/Title (If enforcement activity were narrowing toward more serious cases, the share of detainees with convictions would be expected to rise over the course of the administration. The data shows the opposite. In the administration's first partial month, roughly half of those booked into detention had no conviction; by mid-2026, that share had risen to nearly three-quarters, while the share with violent convictions fell from 4.3 percent to 1.7 percent over the same period. This pattern is consistent with an enforcement approach driven by aggregate arrest targets rather than one prioritizing the most serious cases, a dynamic also reflected in reporting on internally set arrest quotas.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1063 0 R
/Next 1072 0 R
>>
endobj
